 # pyHPSU MQTT Integration Crontab Configuration
  #
  # This file contains example crontab entries for automated MQTT data publishing
  # from the pyHPSU heat pump monitoring system.
  #
  # Installation:
  # 1. Copy the desired lines below
  # 2. Edit crontab: crontab -e
  # 3. Paste and modify as needed
  # 4. Save and exit

  # Standard MQTT publishing (every 5 minutes)
  # Publishes individual sensor values to separate MQTT topics
  # Target: Local MQTT broker (192.168.0.106)
  */5 * * * * /home/pi/pyHPSU/mqtt-integration/scripts/hpsu_mqtt_all.sh >/dev/null 2>&1

  # Custom parametric MQTT publishing (every minute except multiples of 5)
  # Publishes complete JSON payload to single MQTT topic
  # Target: External MQTT server (configurable)
  # Usage: script <MQTT_HOST> <MQTT_PORT> <TOPIC>
  1-4,6-9,11-14,16-19,21-24,26-29,31-34,36-39,41-44,46-49,51-54,56-59 * * * *
  /home/pi/pyHPSU/mqtt-integration/scripts/hpsu_mqtt_custom.sh 192.168.0.192 1883 /home/sensors >/dev/null 2>&1

  # Alternative configurations:

  # Single MQTT server (every 5 minutes) - use only one of the above
  # */5 * * * * /home/pi/pyHPSU/mqtt-integration/scripts/hpsu_mqtt_custom.sh 192.168.0.192 1883 /home/sensors >/dev/null 2>&1

  # High frequency monitoring (every minute) - use with caution, may overload CAN bus
  # * * * * * /home/pi/pyHPSU/mqtt-integration/scripts/hpsu_mqtt_custom.sh 192.168.0.192 1883 /home/sensors >/dev/null 2>&1

  # Notes:
  # - Ensure scripts have executable permissions: chmod +x /home/pi/pyHPSU/mqtt-integration/scripts/*.sh
  # - Monitor system load when using high frequency polling
  # - The timing configuration above prevents CAN bus conflicts between scripts
  # - Adjust IP addresses and topics according to your MQTT broker setup
